course: dictionary
lesson: 4838
title: Vocabulary in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hydrangea is a garden bush with big round heads made of lots of small flowers. Its flowers can be blue, pink, purple or white.
explain: «Hydrangeas growing in acidic soil take in aluminium and turn blue.» The sentence gives you the clue: the colour of the flowers depends on the soil the bush grows in.
explain: «In alkaline soil they stay pink, so changing the soil can change the colour.» Alkaline is a new word, but the clues help. Pink flowers grow in it, and it is the other kind of soil from acidic, so it must be the chalky kind. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A hydrangea is a garden bush with large round heads of small flowers.
fact: Hydrangea flowers can be blue, pink, purple or white.
fact: «Hydrangeas turn blue in acidic soil and stay pink in alkaline soil.»
fact: Acidic soil makes hydrangea flowers blue. Chalky, alkaline soil makes them pink.
fact: «A hydrangea bush» and «blue hydrangeas» are useful phrases to know when you read about gardens.
exercise: What is a hydrangea? | A bird that lives near ponds | *A garden bush with large round heads of small flowers | A tall tree that grows in forests | A type of soil, like chalk
exercise: «Hydrangeas turn blue in acidic soil.» What colour are the flowers when the soil is acidic? | Purple, only in winter | White | *Blue | Pink
exercise: Which soil makes hydrangeas stay pink? | Wet soil | *Alkaline soil, which is chalky | Acidic soil
test: In «Hydrangeas turn blue in acidic soil and stay pink in alkaline soil», which word tells you the colour that stays the same? | soil | acidic | *pink | blue
test: Mia's garden bush has big round heads made of tiny flowers. What is it most likely to be? | A pine tree | *A hydrangea | A sunflower | A cactus
exam: What decides the colour of a hydrangea's flowers? | The name the gardener gives it | *The soil it grows in, since acidic soil makes blue and alkaline soil makes pink | The number of leaves on the bush | The sunshine, since bright light makes every flower pink
